$\str{T}$ is a completion of $\str C_n$, however it has no $\mathcal K_{1,3}$-completion. Moreover, every proper substructure of $\str C_n$ (that is, a path consisting of
at most one edge of distance three and others of distance one) does have a $\mathcal K_{1,3}$-completion.
It follows that there is no $n(\str{T})$ and thus $\mathcal K_{1,3}$ is not a locally finite subclass of $\mathcal R$.

